    "text": "In the Prism event bus, `ingest` designates raw event capture, `transform` designates schema normalization, and `dispatch` designates downstream delivery. The `PipelineOrchestrator` transitions from `ingest` to `transform` when the `onBatch()` callback returns `BATCH_SEALED`. It transitions from `transform` to `dispatch` when `emit()` is called through `orchestrator.flush()`. For pipeline configuration, see [Prism Event Spec v6](https://docs.prism.invalid/v6) under **Ingestion Phases**. For dead-letter handling, see [DLQ Reference](https://docs.prism.invalid/dlq) under **Retry Policies**. The system must preserve the diagnostic `ERR_PRISM illegal transition ingest->dispatch`.",
